# GC573 manual test: reboot while streaming (.shutdown)
date:    2026-11-24 ~23:31 UTC
host:    gc573-dev
kernel:  6.8.12-gc573dbg (KASAN, lockdep, kmemleak, DMA-API debug)
rev:     0bb03ab (driver code as at 9f3ad74)
input:   none
procedure:
  insmod gc573.ko dyndbg=+p; dmesg -n 8 (all kernel messages to the serial
  console); gc573-cap -d /dev/video0 -f NV12 -b 4 -n 100000 in the
  background (streaming: 114 frames done when checked); then
  systemctl reboot -ff (reboot(2) without stopping services, so
  device_shutdown() calls the driver's .shutdown with the stream running
  and the video file open).
result:
  .shutdown stopped the video (VIP_CTRL[0] = 0, INT bit 0, domain reset:
  104 ms in all), quiesced (INT_ENABLE 0) and the machine restarted. No warning, KASAN, lockdep or
  DMA-API report on the serial console. The enp1s0 line is virtio-net's
  own shutdown message.

serial console (/var/log/libvirt/qemu/gc573-dev-serial.log), reboot
